---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import CephCapacityCalculator from '../../../components/tools/CephCapacityCalculator.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Ceph Storage Capacity Calculator (EC & Replication) | InfraOpsX"
  description="Estimate Ceph raw and theoretical usable storage for replication and erasure coding (EC), plus efficiency, overhead, and reserve-based planning capacity—not MAX AVAIL."
  lang="en"
  canonicalPath="/tools/ceph-capacity-calculator/"
  enPath="/tools/ceph-capacity-calculator/"
  zhPath="/zh/tools/ceph-capacity-calculator/"
  pagefindType="Tool"
>
  <Header locale="en" switchHref="/zh/tools/ceph-capacity-calculator/" />

  <main class="tool-detail-shell" data-pagefind-body>
    <div class="container tool-detail-container">
      <div class="tools-breadcrumb" data-pagefind-ignore>
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <a href="/tools/">Tools</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span>Ceph Capacity Calculator</span>
      </div>

      <header class="tool-detail-header">
        <span class="section-label">CEPH · CAPACITY PLANNING</span>
        <h1>Ceph Storage Capacity Calculator</h1>
        <p>Estimate raw, theoretical usable, and planning capacity for replicated and erasure-coded (EC) Ceph storage.</p>
        <p class="tool-intro-note">Enter your OSD count, capacity per OSD, and protection layout. If you do not know your CRUSH failure domain, leave the optional Advanced check closed.</p>
      </header>

      <section class="tool-section" aria-labelledby="calculator-heading">
        <div class="tool-section-heading">
          <span class="section-label">CALCULATOR</span>
          <h2 id="calculator-heading">Plan Ceph capacity before deployment.</h2>
        </div>
        <div data-pagefind-ignore>
          <CephCapacityCalculator locale="en" />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="tool-info-grid">
        <article class="tool-info-card">
          <span class="section-label">HOW IT WORKS</span>
          <h2>Use the layout that matches your data protection model.</h2>
          <p>Raw capacity is OSD count × capacity per OSD (assuming equal-size OSDs). For replication, theoretical usable = raw / replication size; for EC, theoretical usable = raw × k / (k + m). Planning capacity is theoretical usable × (1 − your chosen Reserve %). See the <a href="https://docs.ceph.com/en/squid/rados/operations/erasure-code/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ceph erasure-code documentation</a> for the k/m overhead model.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="tool-info-card">
          <span class="section-label">IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS</span>
          <h2>Capacity planning is an estimate.</h2>
          <p>This calculator assumes all included OSDs have the same capacity and are eligible for the selected pool. It does not know OSD utilization, BlueStore/metadata overhead, uneven placement, CRUSH rules, device classes, or recovery requirements. The optional Host/OSD check tests only the basic count required for placement; passing it does <strong>not</strong> verify actual CRUSH placement. Planning capacity is <strong>not</strong> Ceph <code>df</code> <code>MAX AVAIL</code> and does not guarantee safely writable space. For actual pool capacity, inspect <code>ceph df</code> and <code>ceph osd df tree</code>. See <a href="https://docs.ceph.com/en/squid/rados/operations/monitoring/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ceph monitoring documentation</a>.</p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="tool-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
        <span class="section-label">FAQ</span>
        <h2 id="faq-heading">Common questions</h2>
        <details open>
          <summary>What is the difference between TB and TiB?</summary>
          <p>TB uses decimal units: 1 TB = 10<sup>12</sup> bytes. TiB uses binary units: 1 TiB = 2<sup>40</sup> bytes. The calculator keeps your selected unit as the primary display and shows the corresponding decimal or binary unit as a reference.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does the planning capacity equal Ceph MAX AVAIL?</summary>
          <p>No. It subtracts only your chosen planning reserve from theoretical usable capacity. It does not account for current usage, CRUSH distribution, fullness thresholds, BlueStore overhead or recovery headroom. It must not be used as a guarantee of safe available space.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I estimate usable storage for three replicas?</summary>
          <p>With identical OSDs, multiply OSD count by capacity per OSD to get raw capacity, then divide by 3. For example, six 4 TB OSDs yield 24 TB raw and 8 TB theoretical usable. A 15% planning reserve gives 6.8 TB as a planning target, not Ceph MAX AVAIL.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How is Ceph erasure coding (EC) capacity calculated?</summary>
          <p>Use the standard k data chunks and m parity chunks: theoretical usable = raw × k / (k + m). With EC 4+2 and 24 TB raw, theoretical usable is 16 TB. The placement rule must be able to place all six chunks; this tool does not verify the actual CRUSH rule.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What if I have fewer hosts than replicas or EC chunks?</summary>
          <p>Open Advanced, choose Host as the CRUSH failure domain, and enter the number of eligible hosts. The calculator will stop if that count is below the replication size or EC k+m. Passing the count check is only a necessary condition, not proof that the real layout works.</p>
        </details>
      </section>

      <section class="related-tools" data-pagefind-ignore>
        <div>
          <span class="section-label">RELATED TOOLS</span>
          <h2>More infrastructure tools are on the way.</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/tools/">View all tools</a>
      </section>

      <section class="tool-cta" data-pagefind-ignore>
        <div class="cta-box">
          <div>
            <span class="section-label">INFRAOPSX</span>
            <h2>Need help with Ceph or Kubernetes storage?</h2>
            <p>Contact InfraOpsX for practical infrastructure guidance.</p>
          </div>
          <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact InfraOpsX</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer locale="en" />
</BaseLayout>
